      <div id="childContent">
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681690"
      id="7681690"
      data-guid="7681690"
      data-position="3841"
      data-full-title="§ 151-22: General requirements."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681690_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681690_label" for="7681690_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681690"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-22
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681690"
    >
General requirements.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681690" data-guid="7681690"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681690" data-guid="7681690" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681690_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681691"><a alt="151-22A" class="litem_number" href="7681691#7681691" onclick="return false;" title="151-22A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Buildings and parts thereof shall be maintained so as to be capable of sustaining safely their own weight and the loads to which they may be subject.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681692"><a alt="151-22B" class="litem_number" href="7681692#7681692" onclick="return false;" title="151-22B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Buildings shall be maintained so that loads are transmitted to the soil without undue differential settlement, unsafe deformation or movement of the building or any structural part.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681693"><a alt="151-22C" class="litem_number" href="7681693#7681693" onclick="return false;" title="151-22C">C. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Buildings shall be maintained so that protection is provided for all structural members which may become structurally unsound if left unprotected. Causes of such deterioration include, among others, action of freezing and thawing, dampness, corrosion, wetting and drying, and termites or other destructive insects.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681694"><a alt="151-22D" class="litem_number" href="7681694#7681694" onclick="return false;" title="151-22D">D. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Buildings built in soil which is water bearing at any season of the year shall be maintained so that ground- and surface water will not penetrate into habitable spaces, basements and cellars.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681695"
      id="7681695"
      data-guid="7681695"
      data-position="3846"
      data-full-title="§ 151-23: Exterior protection; foundation walls."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681695_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681695_label" for="7681695_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681695"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-23
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681695"
    >
Exterior protection; foundation walls.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681695" data-guid="7681695"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681695" data-guid="7681695" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681695_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681696"><a alt="151-23A" class="litem_number" href="7681696#7681696" onclick="return false;" title="151-23A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">The foundation walls of every structure shall be maintained in good repair and be structurally sound.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681697"><a alt="151-23B" class="litem_number" href="7681697#7681697" onclick="return false;" title="151-23B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Foundation walls shall be considered in good repair and structurally sound if found free from damage or defects and capable of bearing imposed loads.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681698"
      id="7681698"
      data-guid="7681698"
      data-position="3849"
      data-full-title="§ 151-24: Stairs; porches; landings; balconies; fire escapes; railings."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681698_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681698_label" for="7681698_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681698"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-24
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681698"
    >
Stairs; porches; landings; balconies; fire escapes; railings.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681698" data-guid="7681698"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681698" data-guid="7681698" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681698_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681699"><a alt="151-24A" class="litem_number" href="7681699#7681699" onclick="return false;" title="151-24A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">The stairs, porches, landings, balconies, fire escapes, and railings affixed to the exterior of every structure shall be kept in good repair and structurally sound. Railings shall be provided for stairs and balconies and, where necessary, for porches and accessible roofs.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681700"><a alt="151-24B" class="litem_number" href="7681700#7681700" onclick="return false;" title="151-24B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Stairs and porches shall be considered to be in good repair and structurally sound when found to be free of holes, cracks, and capable of supporting imposed loads.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681701"><a alt="151-24C" class="litem_number" href="7681701#7681701" onclick="return false;" title="151-24C">C. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Properly balustraded railings shall be provided when there is clear danger of accident or personal injury and must be capable of bearing normally imposed loads.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681702"
      id="7681702"
      data-guid="7681702"
      data-position="3853"
      data-full-title="§ 151-25: Weatherproof and watertight."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681702_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681702_label" for="7681702_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681702"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-25
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681702"
    >
Weatherproof and watertight.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681702" data-guid="7681702"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681702" data-guid="7681702" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681702_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681703"><a alt="151-25A" class="litem_number" href="7681703#7681703" onclick="return false;" title="151-25A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Every structure used for human habitation shall be so maintained that it will be weatherproof and watertight.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681704"><a alt="151-25B" class="litem_number" href="7681704#7681704" onclick="return false;" title="151-25B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Exterior walls, roofs, and all openings around doors, windows, chimneys, and all other parts of the structure shall be so maintained as to keep water from entering the structure. Damaged materials must be repaired or replaced. All parts of the structure that show evidence of dry rot or other deterioration shall be repaired or replaced and refinished. Such replacement, wherever practical, shall be in conformity with the remainder of the structure.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681705"
      id="7681705"
      data-guid="7681705"
      data-position="3856"
      data-full-title="§ 151-26: Interior protection; free from dampness."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681705_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681705_label" for="7681705_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681705"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-26
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681705"
    >
Interior protection; free from dampness.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681705" data-guid="7681705"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681705" data-guid="7681705" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681705_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681706"><a alt="151-26A" class="litem_number" href="7681706#7681706" onclick="return false;" title="151-26A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Cellars, basements, and crawl spaces shall be reasonably free from dampness to prevent conditions conducive to decay or deterioration of the structure.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681707"><a alt="151-26B" class="litem_number" href="7681707#7681707" onclick="return false;" title="151-26B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Ventilation shall be provided in every basement, cellar and crawl space, by means of windows, openings or vents, or mechanical vents.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681708"
      id="7681708"
      data-guid="7681708"
      data-position="3859"
      data-full-title="§ 151-27: Structural members."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681708_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681708_label" for="7681708_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681708"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-27
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681708"
    >
Structural members.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681708" data-guid="7681708"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681708" data-guid="7681708" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681708_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681709"><a alt="151-27A" class="litem_number" href="7681709#7681709" onclick="return false;" title="151-27A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Supporting structural members, of every structure, shall be structurally sound.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681710"><a alt="151-27B" class="litem_number" href="7681710#7681710" onclick="return false;" title="151-27B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Supporting structural members shall be considered to be structurally sound, if such members are capable of bearing imposed loads safely and if there is no evidence of deterioration.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681711"
      id="7681711"
      data-guid="7681711"
      data-position="3862"
      data-full-title="§ 151-28: Chimneys; flues and vents."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681711_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681711_label" for="7681711_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681711"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-28
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681711"
    >
Chimneys; flues and vents.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681711" data-guid="7681711"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681711" data-guid="7681711" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681711_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681712"><a alt="151-28A" class="litem_number" href="7681712#7681712" onclick="return false;" title="151-28A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Chimneys and all flue and vent attachments thereto, and all other flues and vents, shall be structurally sound and free from defects, to assure the performance of the function for which they are designed and used.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681713"><a alt="151-28B" class="litem_number" href="7681713#7681713" onclick="return false;" title="151-28B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Chimneys, flues, gas vents, or other draft-producing equipment shall provide sufficient draft to develop the rated output of the connected equipment. Chimneys, flue linings where required, flues, gas vents, and their supports shall be structurally safe, durable, smoketight, and capable of withstanding the action of the flue gases.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681714"
      id="7681714"
      data-guid="7681714"
      data-position="3865"
      data-full-title="§ 151-29: Stairs and railings."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681714_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681714_label" for="7681714_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681714"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-29
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681714"
    >
Stairs and railings.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681714" data-guid="7681714"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681714" data-guid="7681714" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681714_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681715"><a alt="151-29A" class="litem_number" href="7681715#7681715" onclick="return false;" title="151-29A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Interior stairs shall be structurally sound and free from defects. Railings shall be provided for stairs, balconies, landings and stairwells.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681716"><a alt="151-29B" class="litem_number" href="7681716#7681716" onclick="return false;" title="151-29B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Treads or risers that evidence excessive wear or are broken, warped or loose shall be repaired. Stairs shall be securely fastened to supporting structural members and be capable of supporting normally imposed loads.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7681717"
      id="7681717"
      data-guid="7681717"
      data-position="3868"
      data-full-title="§ 151-30: Floors, walls and ceilings."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7681717_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7681717_label" for="7681717_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7681717"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 151-30
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7681717"
    >
Floors, walls and ceilings.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7681717" data-guid="7681717"></div>
        <div id="questions-7681717" data-guid="7681717" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7681717_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="7681718"><a alt="151-30A" class="litem_number" href="7681718#7681718" onclick="return false;" title="151-30A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Floors, walls, and ceilings shall be structurally sound.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681719"><a alt="151-30B" class="litem_number" href="7681719#7681719" onclick="return false;" title="151-30B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Floors shall be considered to be structurally sound where capable of safely bearing imposed loads. Walls and ceilings shall be considered to be structurally sound and in good repair when free from breaks, loose plaster and similar conditions.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="7681720"><a alt="151-30C" class="litem_number" href="7681720#7681720" onclick="return false;" title="151-30C">C. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Toilet room and bathroom floors shall be maintained so as to prevent leakage of water through the floor, under normal conditions of use and floor washing, and resultant deterioration or defects in structural members and ceilings below.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
      </div>
  </div>

            </div>
          </div>
        </main>
